{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "brightside-dental-studio-cloudflare",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-10-08",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat", "global_fetch_strictly_public"],
  "triggers": { "crons": ["* * * * *"] },
  "assets": {
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "directory": "./public",
    "run_worker_first": true
  },
  // The `vars` block is the production copy of `.dev.vars`. Wrangler never
  // uploads `.dev.vars` during deploy, so the same values are baked in here
  // instead: `npm run deploy` is a fully configured Worker and the owner
  // dashboard's CSRF protection works immediately after deploy.
  //
  // Why this is intentional (and why the generated `.gitignore` ignores this
  // file even though it carries the production DATABASE_URL, ADMIN_USERNAME,
  // ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH, ADMIN_EMAIL and CSRF_SECRET):
  //   1. Cloudflare Workers need real values at deploy time — `wrangler
  //      deploy` does not read `.dev.vars`, and `wrangler secret put` is a
  //      separate step that asks the operator to type the value into the
  //      terminal. Baking the values into `vars` makes the first deploy
  //      zero-config and keeps the owner dashboard functional.
  //   2. The values are the same ones the operator already typed into the
  //      builder. Treating them as "secrets" only at deploy time and then
  //      committing them to a public repo would be a worse failure mode
  //      than the current one.
  //   3. The generated `.gitignore` already covers `wrangler.jsonc`, so a
  //      customer's first `git init && git add . && git push` does NOT commit
  //      this file. The on-disk file ships only so the Worker can read it.
  //   4. If the operator ever wants true secret management, they can switch
  //      to `wrangler secret put DATABASE_URL`, `wrangler secret put
  //      CSRF_SECRET`, etc., delete the corresponding `vars` entries, and
  //      push the file. The current scaffolding keeps the simpler path.
  //
  // The placeholder value below (the one between the quotes) is replaced at
  // build time by the builder with the actual JSON object: { DATABASE_URL,
  // ADMIN_USERNAME, ADMIN_EMAIL, ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH, CSRF_SECRET }.
  "vars": {
    "DATABASE_URL": "postgresql://carlamissiona:yhxjpBia4MA6@ep-round-moon-a1obo7oq-pooler.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/workers_db",
    "ADMIN_USERNAME": "admin",
    "ADMIN_EMAIL": "missiona.carla@gmail.com",
    "ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH": "pbkdf2$210000$MPw8J_CLurGtJMj19oMUGQ$UgRhztXBS-b4tYrhi2F7SCGp5KhhN3fkMs94ZrMN8xE",
    "CSRF_SECRET": "e20346d1d4b12c6d8ae69d3c1c1a24d6df743d1ce1050fd0d41d3289e4ed95ca"
  },
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
